## Architecture — read this before writing anything

**`notes/*.md` is the only source of truth.** Everything else is a build product:

```
notes/*.md  ──(kg build)──►  .kg/graph.sqlite         nodes, edges, FTS5, embeddings, communities
                          ├─►  .kg/{entities,relations,sources,measurements}.json
                          ├─►  notes/entities/*.md    generated hubs  (kg generate)
                          ├─►  notes/sources/*.md     generated hubs  (kg generate)
                          ├─►  notes/communities/*.md generated summaries (kg communities --write)
                          ├─►  map.md                 generated index  (kg generate)
                          └─►  gaps-report.md         generated report (kg gaps)
```

Never hand-edit `.kg/`. In generated notes, edit only the identity fields (`entity-type`, `aliases`, `tier`, `authors`, `url`, `year`) and the analyst prose inside `<!-- ANALYST SUMMARY -->` markers — those are preserved across regeneration. Everything else in them is rebuilt.

Delete `.kg/` any time. `kg build` recreates it.

