## Frontmatter contract

```yaml
---
note-type: claim            # concept | claim | question | source | entity | community
title: "..."
aliases: ["..."]
status: seed                # seed | draft | verified | stale | disputed  (question: open | researching | answered)
confidence: 0.5             # 0–1
tags: [{{FIRST_ANGLE}}]     # first tag is the research angle
created: YYYY-MM-DD
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
review-after: YYYY-MM-DD

about: ["[[stem|Display]]"]     # typed relations: list-of-link, one key per predicate
evidence: ["[[handle|Source: handle]]"]

asserted-by: agent          # agent | user | source
extraction-run: YYYY-MM-DD-<label>
---
```

Relation properties must be **lists of wikilink strings**. That exact shape is what the compiler detects as an edge, what the graph view follows, and what Breadcrumbs renders. A bare string or a list of plain names compiles to nothing and errors nowhere.

`notes/_meta/schema.md` carries the full contract, including the generated predicate table.

