## The `kg` command surface

```
kg build        notes → .kg/*.json + graph.sqlite     (incremental)
kg generate     graph → entity/source hubs + map.md
kg doctor       link resolution + invariants + readiness      ← THE GATE
kg embed        embed changed notes
kg search "<q>" [--k] [--type] [--hops]
kg context "<q>" [--budget 8000]                       ← call this instead of grepping
kg neighbors <note> [--predicate] [--depth]
kg path <a> <b> | kg subgraph <note> [--format md|mermaid|canvas]
kg communities [--write] [--min-size 3]
kg gaps | kg contradictions | kg eval
kg ingest <path|url>
```

Run as `python3 -m scripts.kg <cmd>` from this directory. Seven are also served over MCP via `.mcp.json`, so tools are available with no setup.

**Use `kg context`, not grep.** It fuses BM25 and vector search, expands along weighted graph edges, lifts in cluster summaries, and returns a token-budgeted pack where every block carries its source and confidence.

